.TH ENSURE-IDENTITY 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ensure-identity \- package service-identity lifecycle reconciler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ensure-identity
.RI [ --disable ] " " FRAGMENT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ensure-identity
is invoked only from makepkg-generated package scripts with the
package's own
.I accounts.d
fragment, never by hand. Ensure mode (post-install, post-upgrade)
creates every declared group, user, locked shadow entry and state
directory; it never modifies, reorders, or rehashes anything already
present, converges identical redeclarations, and refuses same-name
or same-ID conflicts loudly. Disable mode
.RB ( --disable ,
post-deinstall) sanitizes without deleting: it locks shadow entries
and forces nologin shells while preserving UIDs, GIDs, homes,
groups, state directories and history (IDs are never recycled).
Absent entries are silent no-ops, so repeats are harmless.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --disable
Sanitize mode for package removal (default is ensure mode).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/saphira/accounts.d/
Per-package declaration fragments (the single source of truth).
.TP
.I /usr/share/saphira/accounts.tsv
Base-seed reservations (authority file, not the reconciler).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Reconciled (or nothing to do).
.TP
.B 1
Conflict, malformed fragment, unusable credential, or misuse.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
ensure-identity /usr/share/saphira/accounts.d/dbus
.br
ensure-identity --disable /tmp/saphira-identity.XXXXXX
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR recipe (5),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-repo-state (8),
.BR saphira-repo-migrate (8)
